<type>(<scope>): <specific change in imperative form>

Summary
- <What changed and the user/developer outcome.>

Problem and rationale
- <Previous behavior, concrete failure/need, why this approach.>

Changes
- Added: <Behavior, components, safeguards; or None with reason.>
- Changed: <Behavior and important implementation details.>
- Removed: <What became unnecessary and its replacement; or None.>
- Reused/simplified: <Existing capability reused and complexity removed.>

File ledger
Path | Action | Purpose and reason | LOC
<repo/path> | <Added/Edited/Removed/Renamed/Copied/Mode changed/Type changed> | <Specific explanation> | +<added> -<deleted> LOC
Totals: <files> files; <action counts>; +<added> -<deleted> LOC; net <delta>.
Generated/lockfile subtotal: +<added> -<deleted> LOC; or None.
Non-text changes: <Binary/LFS/submodule/mode details; or None.>

Verification
- Validated tree: <full staged tree object ID>.
- Comparison base: <full parent/base commit ID, or EMPTY TREE for first commit>.
- Environment: <OS/architecture, toolchain versions, lockfile identity/configuration>.
- <Exact command> | PASS | <Actual counts/targets/results> | <Duration>.
- Functional checks: <Critical paths, devices/method, observed outcome>.
- Evidence: <Stable sanitized report location/run ID, timestamp/time zone>.
- Gate: PASS; all required checks completed for this snapshot.

Decisions and ADRs
- <Decision, alternatives, reason, tradeoff, ADR path/status; or None with reason.>

Dependencies and downloads
- <Added/updated/removed name/version; source, purpose, license, integrity,
  scope/data impact and record path. Include deliberate temporary downloads.>
- <If none, explicitly state none; distinguish locked dependency restoration.>

Compatibility, security, and operations
- <API/data/platform compatibility; privacy/permissions; migration/deployment
  impact; measured performance changes or No performance claim.>

Not included and remaining risks
- <Deferred work, reason, impact and tracking reference; or None.>
- <Known non-blocking limitation and mitigation; or None.>

Next steps
1. <Specific follow-up, dependency, acceptance criterion and owner if known.>

Rollback
- <How to undo safely, migration/data consequences, verification afterward.>

References
- <Relevant issues, specifications, ADRs and evidence; no invented identifiers.>

# Replace every placeholder. Retain every section; use None/N/A with a reason.
# No email address is required in the message; keep personal addresses out.
# Delete these instructions and unused trailer examples before committing.
# Optional real trailers belong at the very end, separated by one blank line.
# Refs: <existing issue reference>
# BREAKING CHANGE: <affected consumers and required migration>
